  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;LUCIUS CALPURNIUS PISO CAESONINUS (CONSUL 112 BC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC) was a Roman statesman and general, serving as consul in 112 BC with Marcus Livius Drusus. He was also a legate to Lucius Cassius Longinus in 107 BC."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUCIUS CALPURNIUS PISO CAESONINUS (CONSUL 148 BC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 148 BC) was the father of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC), serving as consul in 148 BC."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MARCUS LIVIUS DRUSUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Marcus Livius Drusus was a Roman politician and consul in 112 BC, serving alongside Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC)."(&lt;SEP&gt;"Marcus Livius Drusus was a Roman politician and consul in 112 BC, serving alongside Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC)."()</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUCIUS CASSIUS LONGINUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lucius Cassius Longinus was a Roman consul sent into Gaul to oppose the Cimbri and their allies in 107 BC, where he served as the consul with Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate&lt;SEP&gt;"Lucius Cassius Longinus was a Roman consul sent into Gaul to oppose the Cimbri and their allies in 107 BC, where he served as the consul with Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate)."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CIMBRI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Cimbri were a Germanic tribe that posed a military threat to Rome in 107 BC, opposing the Roman army led by Lucius Cassius Longinus and Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate&lt;SEP&gt;"The Cimbri were a Germanic tribe that posed a military threat to Rome in 107 BC, opposing the Roman army led by Lucius Cassius Longinus and Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate)."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TIGURINI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Tigurini were a Celtic tribe that defeated the Roman army in 107 BC, causing the death of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate) and Lucius Cassius Longinus in the battle."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Tigurini were a Celtic tribe that defeated the Roman army in 107 BC, causing the death of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate) and Lucius Cassius Longinus in the battle."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALLOBROGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Allobroges were a Gallic tribe whose territory was the site of the battle in 107 BC where Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate) and Lucius Cassius Longinus fell."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Allobroges were a Gallic tribe whose territory was the site of the battle in 107 BC where Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (legate) and Lucius Cassius Longinus fell."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JULIUS CAESAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Julius Caesar was the father-in-law of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC), who was the grandfather of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Julius Caesar was the father-in-law of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC), who was the grandfather of Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 112 BC)."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPURIUS POSTUMIUS ALBINUS MAGNUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spurius Postumius Albinus Magnus was a Roman politician and consul in 148 BC, serving alongside Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 148 BC)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Spurius Postumius Albinus Magnus was a Roman politician and consul in 148 BC, serving alongside Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul 148 BC)."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUSITANI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Lusitani were a Celtic tribe that defeated Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (praetor) in 154 BC during the Lusitanian War."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Lusitani were a Celtic tribe that defeated Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (praetor) in 154 BC during the Lusitanian War."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THIRD PUNIC WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Third Punic War was a conflict between Rome and Carthage, during which Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul) served as a consul in 148 BC."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Third Punic War was a conflict between Rome and Carthage, during which Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (consul) served as a consul in 148 BC."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEGES CLODIAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Leges Clodiae were laws passed by the Roman Senate, which Cicero violated by executing members of the Cataline conspiracy without a formal trial."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Leges Clodiae were laws passed by the Roman Senate, which Cicero violated by executing members of the Cataline conspiracy without a formal trial."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUINTUS ANCHARIUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quintus Ancharius was a Roman politician who replaced Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus as the governor of Macedonia in 55 BC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quintus Ancharius was a Roman politician who replaced Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus as the governor of Macedonia in 55 BC."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUGUSTUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Augustus was a Roman emperor and a trusted adviser to Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (praefectus urbi) from AD 13 to 32."&lt;SEP&gt;"Augustus was a Roman emperor and a trusted adviser to Lucius Calpurnius Piso Caesoninus (praefectus urbi) from AD 13 to 32."(</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0337-26232cb3bbcb</data>
    </node>
